      "created_at": "2013-02-28T15:14:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Played a game last night against Baron Blade and had two questions come up. &nbsp;</p><p>First, does Twist the Ether stay in play after a villain flips or is it destroyed? &nbsp;</p><p>Second, the player wanted to play Mental Divergence against Paparazzi On the Scene from the Megalopolis environment. &nbsp;Twist the Ether says destroy one ongoing card but the Paparazzi card doesn't have the ongoing keyword. &nbsp;Is it a viable target?</p><p>My reasoning was that it had to have the keyword. &nbsp;They argued that although it doesn't have the ongoing keyword, the effects of the card were still ongoing until the card was destroyed. &nbsp;Wasn't that big an issue, was just looking for some clarification. &nbsp;Thanks.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:30.010Z",
